.TH LEMMINGD 1 "October 2026" "lemmingd 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lemmingd \- selective local-development HTTP and HTTPS proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lemmingd
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B lemmingd firefox
.RI [ options ] " URL"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lemmingd
routes configured domain and path combinations to local development servers or
explicitly allowed remote origins. It can preview a hosting migration in one
proxied browser without changing DNS for a direct browser. It intercepts HTTPS
only for configured domains; all other CONNECT traffic is tunneled unchanged.
Exclusion prefixes take precedence over inclusion prefixes.
.PP
A unique local certificate authority is generated on first start. Normal server
mode does not trust or install it automatically.
.PP
The
.B firefox
command creates or reuses an isolated Firefox profile beside lemmingd's
configuration, configures it to use lemmingd, imports the public CA with
.BR certutil (1),
and launches Firefox with that profile. It does not modify Firefox's default
profile or its profile registry. Firefox is found from PATH, the standard
macOS application locations, or common Windows installation locations. The NSS
tools package is required. On Windows, pass the NSS executable with
.B \-nss-certutil
because the built-in Windows certutil program is incompatible.
.PP
Closing Firefox does not stop lemmingd. Lemmingd does not explicitly close
Firefox when it stops, though terminal-delivered signals can also reach
Firefox. The managed profile retains browser data and remains configured for
the proxy between launches. Lemmingd refuses to modify the profile while
Firefox holds its profile lock. To use the combined command again, close
Firefox and stop any existing lemmingd process first.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Use the specified JSON configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-cacert " path"
Use the specified CA certificate file.
.TP
.BI \-cakey " path"
Use the specified CA private-key file.
.TP
.BI \-listen " host:port"
Override the configured listening address.
.TP
.BI \-firefox-bin " path"
Firefox executable used by the
.B firefox
command.
.TP
.BI \-nss-certutil " path"
NSS certutil executable used by the
.B firefox
command. This is required on Windows unless an NSS certutil is available as
.BR nss-certutil .
.TP
.B \-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lemmingd/config.json
Configuration and redirect rules. Defaults below
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lemmingd/ca.crt
Generated public CA certificate.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lemmingd/ca.key
Generated private CA key. Do not share this file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lemmingd/firefox-profile/
Dedicated Firefox profile created by the
.B firefox
command. It contains profile-local CA trust, cookies, history, sessions, and
other Firefox data. Close Firefox before removing it.
.SH SECURITY
The default listener is 127.0.0.1:18080. Remote clients and non-loopback
redirect targets each require an explicit opt-in. Apply separate network access
controls before enabling either option.
.PP
The managed Firefox profile is private to the operating-system user but can
contain authenticated browsing state. Remove it when that state is no longer
needed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hamsterd (1),
the project README, and SECURITY.md.
